Well, but this highlights a problem with the whole
idea.

You've eliminated the situation where the pet
falls through a hole, the PC dives in after to
"rescue" the pet, but the PC and pet end up far
apart on the same level, or possibly even on
different levels.

Trying to connect up again with your pet before it
goes feral or the PC dies for lack of its help is
one of the fun playing features of the game, and by
making the hole endpoints persistent, you've taken
that out of the game.

PC and pet are both going to end up cheek by jowl
on whatever level they hit. Phooie, that's no fun.

